-- Forced-choice personality pairs, rounds 1-2 of 4 (items 501-550). Authored and
-- AUTHORIZED by the planning thread 2026-08-14 (Peter directive: item content is a
-- decision, planning-level). Design per SPEC Grunt 1: pairs of statements from two
-- DIFFERENT facets (multidimensional pick, Cao & Drasgow 2019 JAP 104:1347-1368),
-- quasi-ipsative structure (Salgado & Tauriz 2014; Salgado, Anderson & Tauriz 2015).
-- Pairing = circulant schedule r=1..4 over the facets ordered by native desirability,
-- so partners sit in the same desirability neighborhood; both statements of a pair are
-- WRITTEN TO the pair's target band (desirability matched by construction, delta 0).
-- Desirability values are author-assigned targets on a 1-9 scale; empirical check
-- later: a statement chosen far above 50% against matched partners is under-matched
-- (future calibration signal from choice rates). Choosing a statement = more of that
-- facet, for every facet including negatively-weighted ones (anger, anxiety,
-- avoid_goal_orientation) -- downstream sign handling is unchanged (negative fit
-- weights; 100-p in commitment). is_active=false: dormant until FC delivery ships.
-- Section + response_format CHECKs widened in migration fc_items_widen_section_and_format_checks.
